From ef67c2584374ab87f62927a1d47b11bbbc2c2641 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:42:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 160/174] tls, dns: fixes from the review of the fallback and
 of ipv6_if_no_ipv4

- The choice of the fallback is written to the cache file in the background,
  not under the lock every dial of the outbound takes, and only when the
  choice of a path changes or gets old: two local addresses with choices of
  their own (two uplinks) no longer rewrite it by turns.
- What a dial made during a rest got through with (the configured
  fingerprint as it is when nothing has worked) is no longer written as the
  choice for the server.
- The first candidate is left on a failure of any kind while it has not
  worked: it is not the configured fingerprint, which the rule protected.
- The same ClientHello is not tried twice: random may have taken firefox.
- The A question of ipv6_if_no_ipv4 goes with the address check of the rule:
  an answer the rule refuses is not cached and tells nothing.
